SUMMARY:Strawberry Gap and Trombatore trails\, 10 mile Fitness Hike.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**This will be a strenuous out and
  back hike of about 10.1 miles and 2\,400 feet of elevation gain ( level 8
 \\*) as we hike up the Eastern Contential Divide**. We will pass through t
 hick rhododendrons and mountain laurels\, pass large boulders and experien
 ce long-range views at Ferguson Peak and the Blue Ridge Pasture\, and cont
 inue with a forest hike on the Trombatore Trail.\nWe begin with a steep cl
 imb on the well-maintained Strawberry Gap trail. At \\~2.5 miles\, we will
  enter the open Blue Ridge Pastures for long range views and connect to th
 e Trombatore forest trail. We will turn around at the end of the Trombator
 e Trail\, with a snack/water break of \\~15 minutes.\n\n**PACE**: This hik
 e will be at a brisk pace (between 2.5-3.3 mi/hr) adjusting for steepness 
 of grade and/or rugged trail conditions\, brief regrouping as needed. This
  10 mile level 8 fitness oriented hike of 2400 feet gain is for conditione
 d hikers. Join us If you like fitness oriented hike workouts.\n\n**Dogs ar
 e not permitted** on this trail\, as it is on private property. Please res
 pect landowner rules...."\n\n**Carpool: 8:30 am to meet at the East Ashevi
 lle Home Depot parking area on the left side upper parking lot adjacient t
 o the upper enterance road. Post if you plan to meet us there\, otherwise 
 see you at the trailhead.**\n\n**Predicted Temperatures** **during Hike Ho
 urs:** sun/clouds @ 70-81 degrees mild winds@ 4 mph\n\n**Cancelation:** wi
 ll be posted on or before 7am hike day.\n\n**DIRECTIONS** to TRAILHEAD: Fr
 om Asheville\, take US74-A (Alt 74)\, also known as Fairview Road or Old C
 harlotte Highway) towards Gerton. Parking lot is on the right a short dist
 ance after crossing over the Eastern Contential Divide.\n\nIF YOU SIGN ON 
 THIS HIKE AND CHANGE YOU MIND (EVEN IF YOU ARE ON THE WAITLIST) GO BACK TO
  THE RSVP LINK AND CHANGE YOUR STATUS TO FREE UP YOUR RESERVED SPOT.\n\n**
 *\\*Hike Levels:*** *Level 1\; 300-600 feet elevation gain\; Level 2 600-9
 00'\; Level 3\, 900-1200"\; Level 4\; 1200-1500' Level 5\; 1500-1800' LEVE
 L 6\; 1800-2100' Level 7*\; 2100-2400' **Level 8\; 2400-2700**' Level 9\; 
 2700-3000' Level 10\; 3000-4000'\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe organiz
 er of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function 
 of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or particip
 ate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to
  assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses and damages arising from\, as a 
 result of and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledging 
 that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
