SUMMARY:Sam Branch Creek Scramble - 4 Waterfalls
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis is one of the steepest rock s
 crambles in the area. We will not be on a trail most of the time\, but in 
 the creek\, climbing up rocks. Most of the creek seems to be a continuous 
 waterfall. Both the Lower and the Upper Falls are spectacular to see. And 
 the views looking across the Shining Rock Wilderness are something to reme
 mber.\nIf you are confident when scrambling up and down rocks and walking 
 in the water you will be welcome to join us. This is the first time I have
  offered to lead this hike for the group. The four waterfalls are Sunburst
  Falls\, Lower Sam Branch\, Upper Sam Branch\, and Wash Hollow Falls.\nWe 
 will do this as an up and back. Elevation gain is approximately 1\,600 fee
 t and the distance is approx. 4 miles.\nWe do not expect a large group of 
 participants since not everyone would like this challenge. We will meet at
  the Sam Knob Parking Lot at the end of Black Balsam Knob Road (FS 816) at
  10 AM. We will shuttle from there to the hike commencement near Sunburst 
 Falls (35.338265\, -82.903358) on State Hwy 215.\n\nThis Asheville Hiking 
 Group event may involve risks to oneself and property. Participants\, by j
 oining this hike\, affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical
  conditioning\, equipment and supplies. Neither your hike organizer nor th
 e Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate risks or be responsible for your we
 ll-being. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damag
 es\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315346294
 /
