SUMMARY:Buck Springs Lodge from Pisgah Inn - 3 Mi\, 500 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 3 Miles\, 500 Ft 
 elevation gain\n* Carpool meeting time is 9:00 at the Asheville Outlets pa
 rking lot behind the Waffle House.\n* Sign up starts Sunday at 8pm\n\nThis
  is a short hike but has some spectacular views. This is rated as a easy h
 ike in AllTrails. We will likely add an out and back portion to another ov
 erlook but will decide that during the hike. Adventurers can add 2.4 miles
  and go to Mt Pisgah. I will try to accommodate several options within thi
 s one hike depending on interest. There are markers along the trail that e
 xplore the history of the Bucks Spring Lodge. It is a bit of a drive at ab
 out 30 minutes from the Asheville Outlets but a pretty drive up the Parkwa
 y.\n\nI enjoy stopping at the Pisgah Inn after the hike and sitting in the
  rocking chairs behind the hotel. They have a convenience store where you 
 can buy drinks and sandwiches or you can bring your own. We will try to br
 eak up into cars that want to do that and want to just go back to the carp
 ool area.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/north-carolina/buck-spring
 -trail--2\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will meet at the Asheville Outlets behind the
  Waffle House at 9:00. Please be there a little early so we can leave at 9
 :00 for the trailhead. If you plan to meet us at the Pisgah Inn parking lo
 t\, plan to be there by 9:30.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and p
 ost a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of pr
 ecipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 9:
 00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text 
 or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nT
 his Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transpor
 tation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their
  own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical co
 nditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself
  and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can 
 assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full respo
 nsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
